#ROOM
Vnum     51200
Name     Veyran Technical Academy~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     You have arrived at Veyran Technical Academy, a training station in orbit
above TRAPPIST-1 e. This academy teaches the basic commands needed to survive,
travel and interact with other people in the wider interstellar community.
Each compartment has a specific lesson. Explore the academy in full and read
each room carefully. The student message area is to the west; return here
afterward and continue north when you are ready.

The entrance concourse reflects its builders: dense modular machinery, exposed
service trunks and compact multi-level workspaces. Through the nearest
observation panel you can see TRAPPIST-1 e below, with neighbouring worlds
occasionally visible against the dark.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51201
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51330
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51201
Name     Veyran Instruction Spine~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor links the academy's first instructional rooms. The language and
communication lesson is to the west, while practical skill instruction is to
the east. When you have finished with both rooms, return here and continue
north.

The passage is built around dense modular machinery, exposed service trunks
and compact multi-level workspaces, with bright task lighting surrounded by
dense fields of status indicators. Displays along the wall present Veyran
engineering diagrams, prototype housings and celebrated technical
breakthroughs.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51203
Desc      The Laboratory of Skills.
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51200
Desc      Entrance to Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51206
Desc      Abbigayle's Language Lessons.
~
#ENDEXIT

#MUDPROG
Progtype  leave_prog~
Arglist   100~
Comlist   if isimmort($n)
else
  mpforce $n vis
endif
~
#ENDPROG

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51202
Name     Veyran Navigation Success Annex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     You completed the navigation exercise successfully. Continue north to return
to the reference room and resume the academy course.

A small window in this quiet annex looks toward TRAPPIST-1 e, a reminder that
the entire training complex is an orbital station.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51203
Name     Veyran Skills Laboratory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This is the academy's practical skills laboratory. Type PRACTICE to see the
abilities currently available to you. Your list may include weapon skills,
general skills, languages and other advanced abilities. To improve something,
use PRACTICE <full skill name>.

For example, to practice dual wield, type PRAC DUAL WIELD. Additional
proficiency is gained through training and successful use. Type HELP PRACTICE
or HELP <skill> whenever you need more information.

Veyran instructors favor a Veyran approach that rewards preparation, clever
equipment use and rapid adaptation. The room itself is equipped with layered
diagnostic consoles, removable panels and accessible service conduits.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51201
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51240 1 51203
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51204
Name     Veyran Reference Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors silence~
Desc     This quiet reference room suppresses most public channels so that students can
read without interruption. Type CHAN for a list of channels. You can disable a
channel with CHAN -<channel>, enable it with CHAN +<channel>, or use CHAN -ALL
and CHAN +ALL to silence or restore them together.

When you are ready, go west for the navigation exercise. Follow the room
descriptions until you find your way back here. If you become lost, the up
route returns you to this room. Once you have completed the exercise, continue
north.

The archive contains Veyran engineering diagrams, prototype housings and
celebrated technical breakthroughs. bright task lighting surrounded by dense
fields of status indicators keeps the room comfortable for long periods of
study.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51214
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51201
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51207
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51205
Name     Veyran Combat Trials Control~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     This chamber is reserved for controlled combat trials. In ordinary play you
will encounter mobiles, often shortened to MOBS. Some may be aggressive and
attack as soon as you enter their location. Defeating opponents can provide
experience and loot.

After a fight, EXAMINE CORPSE and GET ALL CORPSE can be used to inspect and
recover items. CONFIG +AUTOLOOT and related configuration options can automate
parts of this process. REST, SLEEP, WAKE and STAND are useful while recovering
between exercises.

The chamber is arranged around a Veyran approach that rewards preparation,
clever equipment use and rapid adaptation, with dense modular machinery,
exposed service trunks and compact multi-level workspaces protecting the rest
of the station from the training area.
~
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51206
Name     Veyran Language and Culture Suite~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This room teaches the language system. Type PRACTICE to see languages
available to you. Your native tongue and the common language are normally
available without additional study. To learn another language, use LANGUAGE
LEARN <language>.

For more information use HELP LANGUAGES, HELP SPEAK and HELP TONGUE. Language
study consumes practice sessions, and capable students generally learn more
efficiently.

The walls carry Veyran engineering diagrams, prototype housings and celebrated
technical breakthroughs, giving students examples of how language, history and
identity developed among the Veyran.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51201
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51294 1 51206
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51207
Name     Veyran Orientation Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is the beginning of the navigation exercise. Type CONFIG +AUTOEXIT if you
want obvious exits displayed automatically. EXIT lists visible routes, and
LOOK <direction> lets you inspect an adjoining direction before moving.

Your next route is west. Try EXIT and LOOK WEST before moving on. The exercise
uses dense modular machinery, exposed service trunks and compact multi-level
workspaces to make each section visually distinct without changing the
station's underlying layout.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51209
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy, it looks safe
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    Door~
ExDesc       You see a solid oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51208
Name     Veyran Combat Practice Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is a controlled combat practice bay. A restrained training creature is
used here to demonstrate attacking, judging an opponent and withdrawing from a
fight. The CONSIDER command compares your character with a potential opponent;
elsewhere, use CON <MOBNAME> before attacking something unfamiliar.

The bay follows a Veyran approach that rewards preparation, clever equipment
use and rapid adaptation. Heavy barriers and layered diagnostic consoles,
removable panels and accessible service conduits keep the exercise isolated
from the inhabited sections of the station.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51216
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51245 1 51208
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51209
Name     Veyran Sealed-Access Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This section teaches doors and less-obvious exits. A closed door may not be
listed among obvious exits until you interact with it. Read the room
description, LOOK <direction>, try moving into a direction, and use OPEN
<direction> or OPEN DOOR when appropriate. HELP OPEN provides more detail.

bright task lighting surrounded by dense fields of status indicators and
deliberately repetitive wall panels make the exercise depend on observation
rather than decoration.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51210
Desc      An Enclosed Room
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51207
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51211
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51209 0 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see a solid oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51210
Name     Veyran Discovery Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     You found the enclosed chamber. Hidden or closed rooms like this appear
throughout the game, sometimes with obvious clues and sometimes with very
subtle ones. LOOK, EXIT and careful reading are your most reliable tools.

The compact chamber uses dense modular machinery, exposed service trunks and
compact multi-level workspaces. Its plain construction is intentional: the
lesson is to notice access routes rather than rely on elaborate scenery.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51209
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51210 2 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51211
Name     Veyran Hidden-Route Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This passage introduces special and hidden exits. Hidden routes may not be
found simply by walking into every wall. Read descriptions, inspect mobiles
and objects, and look for words that might identify a door or route.

Locked exits may require a key or an appropriate skill. Directions can be
abbreviated as N, E, W, S, NE, NW, SE, SW, U and D. Some special routes use a
word such as LEAVE, CLIMB or ENTER. Continue north and use the next room's
description to find the concealed route.

The Veyran design language here uses dense modular machinery, exposed service
trunks and compact multi-level workspaces, making small visual details
especially important.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51212
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51209
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51212
Name     Veyran Heritage Salon~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This chamber has been furnished as a Veyran heritage salon. A broad table and
twelve seats dominate the center while exhibits of Veyran engineering
diagrams, prototype housings and celebrated technical breakthroughs line the
walls. One wall display appears slightly different from the others.

Use LOOK <word> on details mentioned in the room. Sometimes inspecting one
object reveals the clue needed to discover a hidden exit. The exercise is
unchanged mechanically; only the station's cultural presentation differs.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51211
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51213
Desc      door
~
Keywords  tapestry door~
Flags     isdoor closed secret~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51212 3 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    tapestry~
ExDesc       Upon closer inspection you realise that this is not even a tapestry, but
a cunningly camouflaged wall! You can see the outline of a door as you
look closer.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    west~
ExDesc       You see a tapestry on the wall here, something just isn't right about it.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    w~
ExDesc       You see a tapestry on the wall.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see a cleverly disguised door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    Crystal globes~
ExDesc       This globes cast shadows in the corners. The shadows on the west
tapestry almost appears to be an opening.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51213
Name     Veyran Maintenance Alcove~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     You found the concealed alcove. Secret rooms can contain useful items, clues
or alternate routes, so careful reading often pays off. This room also
demonstrates a special SOMEWHERE exit. Inspect the picture and nearby wall if
you want to discover the intended route, or use the obvious up exit to return.

The alcove exposes layered diagnostic consoles, removable panels and
accessible service conduits, giving the space the feel of a hidden service
compartment inside Veyran Technical Academy.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51212
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction somewhere~
ToRoom    51202
Keywords  crack~
Flags     hidden auto~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51213 1 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see an oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    picture~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    crack~
ExDesc       This is a huge CRACK, you could probably squeeze through it. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    wall~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51214
Name     Veyran Readiness Concourse~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor introduces commands used to inspect your character. SCORE shows
core statistics, EQUIPMENT lists worn items, INVENTORY shows carried items,
and LEVEL reports advancement information. Common abbreviations include SC, EQ
and I.

Use HELP <subject> for additional information. The concourse is finished with
dense modular machinery, exposed service trunks and compact multi-level
workspaces, and bright task lighting surrounded by dense fields of status
indicators clearly marks the route toward combat training.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51215
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51204
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51215
Name     Veyran Combat Briefing Deck~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Combat training is immediately ahead. You can begin an ordinary fight with
KILL <mob>, while many learned skills and abilities can also initiate combat.
Before attacking unfamiliar opponents, use CONSIDER and review the help for
your available abilities.

Remember that aggressive actions against another player can have consequences.
The briefing deck reflects a Veyran approach that rewards preparation, clever
equipment use and rapid adaptation; layered diagnostic consoles, removable
panels and accessible service conduits monitors the practice bay below.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51217
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51214
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    51216
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51216
Name     Veyran Withdrawal Training Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     This bay explains ways to leave a dangerous fight. WIMPY can automatically
withdraw you when your hit points fall below a chosen threshold. FLEE attempts
an immediate manual withdrawal. Emergency recall or extraction mechanics may
also exist, but they generally carry a greater cost and should be treated as a
last resort.

The room is intentionally austere, with dense modular machinery, exposed
service trunks and compact multi-level workspaces and clear route markers
designed to make emergency instructions easy to understand.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51208
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51215
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51217
Name     Veyran Recovery Lounge~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Long fights and long journeys require recovery. REST is the safest ordinary
way to recover. SLEEP can recover more deeply but leaves you vulnerable in
unsafe locations. Use WAKE after sleeping and STAND after resting.

Characters can also become hungry or thirsty. Ask the service unit here for
food or a canteen, then use EAT <item> or DRINK <item>. The fountain can also
be used directly or to refill a container.

This is a compact workshop-commons where tables double as repair benches and
study stations. Beyond the windows lies TRAPPIST-1 e below, with neighbouring
worlds occasionally visible against the dark.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51227
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51215
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 51215 1 51217
Reset M 0 51265 1 51217
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51218
Name     Veyran Object Interaction Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Some items that initially appear unimportant can become useful later. Speak
with the student here and pay attention to what they have found.

Containers can hold other objects. Use LOOK IN <container>, GET <item> FROM
<container>, PUT <item> IN <container>, and OPEN <container> when necessary.

Hint: say hello. The exercise occupies a small Veyran student annex fitted
with layered diagnostic consoles, removable panels and accessible service
conduits.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51222
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51242 1 51218
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51219
Name     Veyran Fabrication Loft~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Some objects are obtained by manipulating, combining or crafting other
objects. Your character may eventually learn specialized crafting skills;
other situations are as simple as opening a container or operating a control.

This compact fabrication loft is dense with layered diagnostic consoles,
removable panels and accessible service conduits. It mirrors the practical
working style found throughout Veyran Technical Academy.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    51222
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 51218 1 51219
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51220
Name     Veyran Salvage Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A common way to acquire equipment is to recover it from defeated mobiles.
After defeating the training unit here, use EXAMINE CORPSE to inspect what it
carried and GET ALL FROM CORPSE to recover the contents. Configuration options
can automate looting or currency collection.

The salvage exercise takes place in a reinforced work cell equipped with
layered diagnostic consoles, removable panels and accessible service conduits
and arranged according to a Veyran approach that rewards preparation, clever
equipment use and rapid adaptation.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51222
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51260 1 51220
  Reset E 1 51201 1 8
  Reset E 1 51202 1 13
  Reset G 1 51204 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51221
Name     Veyran Academy Supply Exchange~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Shops are useful for acquiring equipment and selling items you no longer need.
LIST shows a merchant's stock, BUY <object> purchases something, SELL <object>
offers an item for sale, and VALUE <object> asks what the merchant will pay.

The backpack is particularly useful because it can hold spare equipment. This
supply exchange is decorated with Veyran engineering diagrams, prototype
housings and celebrated technical breakthroughs and uses layered diagnostic
consoles, removable panels and accessible service conduits for inventory and
transaction handling.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51222
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51270 1 51221
  Reset G 1 51217 1
  Reset G 1 51211 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51222
Name     Veyran Equipment Acquisition Lab~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Finding better equipment is an important part of progression. Some methods
become available only after learning the appropriate skills, including SEARCH
and DIG. Other methods may carry legal or social consequences.

The rooms east, west, above and below demonstrate different ways to obtain
useful items. Explore all four, then continue north.

This equipment lab uses dense modular machinery, exposed service trunks and
compact multi-level workspaces; lockers and work surfaces are sized and
arranged for Veyran trainees.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51223
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51220
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51227
Flags     isdoor~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51221
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51219
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
